build/
# cargo's output for the Rust port on Windows (docs/rust.md; WSL builds elsewhere).
target/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.swp
*.swo
*.DS_Store
CMakeUserPresets.json
legacy-scaffold-*.zip

# Python's bytecode cache, written beside a tools/*.py module that another
# script imports: a by-product of running the tools, never source.
__pycache__/

# Running the application against a sample writes a backup beside its project.
# The samples are inputs, not working directories.
samples/*/backups/

# Third-party reference material under its author's own licence, kept on disk
# and never in the repository: the reference customisation in the legacy
# formats (two style libraries and two survey code files, with their colour
# table), which the tracked resources/customisation/nsw.customisation.json was
# made from. Neither the build, the program nor the tests read anything here.
docs/12d Refrence Files/

# The TfNSW Utility Schema and Specification workbook (DMS-FT-493), under
# TfNSW's licence: kept on disk, never in the repository. The cli.utility_check
# tests read it when it is there (tests/cli/CMakeLists.txt) and are not
# registered when it is not; tools/utility_schema_domains.py reads any copy.
docs/TfNSW Reference Files/

# Not ignored, on purpose: resources/customisation/nsw.customisation.json, a
# customisation compiled into the programs (crates/katana_cad/build.rs). It
# is tracked, committed on the owner's decision of 2026-10-08, and it is the one
# file derived from the reference files above that is: the converter of the
# legacy formats made it from them (docs/customisation.md, "The reference
# customisation"), less the notice text the converter copied into its `notice`
# member, which the owner removed. The reference files stay ignored.
# .gitattributes keeps its bytes the same in every checkout, since it is
# compiled in byte for byte and a customisation kept from it records a digest
# of those bytes.

# Git worktrees created for parallel agents (CLAUDE.md section 8). Each is a
# checkout of its own; tracking one would embed a repository in this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# One developer's own Claude Code files: the permissions they have granted
# here and their private notes. The shared ones - CLAUDE.md,
# .claude/settings.json and .claude/hooks/ - are tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# GDAL's persistent auxiliary metadata: statistics it caches beside a raster
# it has read. A by-product, and a stale one - samples/gis/terrain.asc.aux.xml
# was committed by accident and held approximate statistics the DEM does not
# have (audit IO-13). Katana no longer asks GDAL to write them.
samples/**/*.aux.xml

# The update system's signing keys (docs/update.md): the private halves never enter the
# repository. The public halves are data and ARE committed (cmake/KatanaUpdateKeys.cmake).
# The test keys of tests/update are RFC 8032's published vectors and are kept as hex, never
# as a .pem (tests/update/test_keys.txt).
*.pem
update-signing*
